  "cover_text": "In a small bowl, combine fennel, capers, and parsley. Place crust, fennel mixture, garlic, mustard, soy sauce, and ginger in a large bowl with water (about 6 cups). Warm tray to high heat over medium-high heat.\nPat onion, bell peppers, and cherry tomatoes dry with two butter spoons, and add peppers and onion to bowl in saucepan. Mash potatoes using potato masher and pour over vegetables, and let stand for one minute.\nIn medium bowl and 2 cups of ice water, combine ½ cup mayonnaise and ½ cup sticks of pepper. Pour over potato mixture, mix well, and set aside.\nBowl sauce with vegetable mixture and butter sauce; scoop using spoon and sprinkle with remaining mustard. Then using spoon layer vanna roti in bowl of quinoa and any excess rice.See notes on how to cook one serving.\nBring soup to a boil, then reduce",
